/-!
# `refEnergy` of trial 1 — sharded kernel check (`catalan-410`, peak-RSS)

The one-shot `decide +kernel` proofs of `enc_en1_le` / `enc_en1_ge` needed ~13.8 GB
of peak RSS: a single kernel reduction had to materialise the whole of
`planLits Rm1 Rm1` (nine jobs, each a product of 25 x 25 rational polynomials, then
the log forms) **together with** every `logAbsQ` enclosure and the final accumulation.
The kernel does not reclaim terms inside one reduction, so the peak is essentially
the sum of all intermediates.

The proofs below keep the statements unchanged and split that single reduction into
independent kernel checks, each of which is small:

* `jobN_c0` / `jobN_ts` — one check per job, split further into the constant part
  (`massQ` of the product polynomial) and the four log terms (18 checks);
* `planLits_eq` — assembles the nine literal log forms propositionally
  (`refPlan` reduces structurally, no rational arithmetic);
* `ts_eq` / `c0_eq` / `merge_eq` — the `LF.sumL` and `mergeT` reduction over literals;
* `logN` — one check per distinct enclosure argument (5 checks);
* `encTermsN` — the accumulation with the `logAbsQ` results already verified,
  so each step only multiplies rationals;
* `enc_eq` — the shared value of `LF.enc 7`, used by BOTH bounds (the original
  proofs recomputed it twice).
-/

